        "no_buffer_descriptor": "Only a8null and descriptor mode54..55=0 with nonzero44-bit address calls slaveMemoryFromIOPPhys(address,size), obtains existing IOP memory and constructs a size/address response. Zero address uses local allocation; mode1 uses a different host mapping/reply path. Neither alternative is admitted by current owner.",
        "size": "Native bits44..51 supply units; bit52 set selects4KiB units here. Both actual words select4KiB, coldcount8=32KiB versus eventcount1=4KiB. Native reply reencodes rounded units/address from memory object, not unconditional raw echo.",
        "handleCrashlog": "Complete handleCrashlog calls RTBuddy::onPanic, obtains buffer bytes/mapping, supplies them to CrashlogDecoder, invokes decoding and later panic/reporting machinery. Thus the existing-buffer branch is materially different from service negotiation.",
        "preservation": "Complete crashlog power callback releases local+a8 only for an isAsleep transition where powerStatePreservesMemory(newstate) is false. Predicate returns state<3; state2 preserves the local buffer object. Native init starts with+a8null. Actual runtime+a8 is unobserved and is not inferred from the firmware-provided address.",
        "header": "Native decoder validates a32-byte header with CLHE magic0x434c4845, payload-size bounds and version-byte constraints; CLGH0x434c4748 routes multi-crash parsing. Linux parser likewise requires CLHE header/declared size and bounded sections. A valid postevent capture could support crash diagnosis, but no such reserved buffer capture is currently saved."
      },
      "conclusion": "Actual type1 EP1 event is unresolved between buffer negotiation and crash notification. Native and local Linux retained-buffer semantics make crash notification a concrete possibility; size/address bounds alone cannot qualify a harmless echo. Diagnose postevent reserved buffer/header before proposing any echo kit. No pending HOST reply, successful HOST state, second shutdown or app rejoin is established.",
      "safe_echo_qualified": false,
      "native_current_buffer_object_state_bound": false,
      "current_reserved_buffer_available_in_saved_trial_captures": false
    }
  },
